    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d832">

                <pb facs="0913" n="904" xml:id="pg904"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3331/152</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Uruguayan Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gorri</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Under Secretary of State</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 286</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-03-22">March 22, 1938</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Under Secretary</hi>: With reference to the
                    conversations which have been in progress for the purpose of initiating
                    negotiations to concert a trade agreement with this country, I have the honor to
                    advise Your Excellency that with the aim of advancing the study of the question,
                    the Government of Uruguay again expresses its intention of negotiating a
                    commercial agreement intended to regulate and promote interchange between the
                    two countries.</p>
                <p>To this end, my Government has honored me by authorizing me to continue the
                    conversations with the competent authorities of Your Excellency’s
                    Government.</p>
                <p>I therefore request of Your Excellency that you grant me an audience which will
                    permit me to set forth the desires of my Government, which are in harmony with
                    those expressed on various occasions by His Excellency, Cordell Hull, together
                    with the reasons which lead my Government to state again its desire of arriving
                    at an agreement.</p>
                <p>I avail myself [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">César Gorri</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
